7. PREFERENCE DIRECTION UNDER AN EXACT VALUE FUNCTION  (2-10 regime)
========================================================================
  re-judging 4999 rows over 4872 states with the exact adaptive tree ...
  done in 108s

    chosen truly better :   4980  (99.6%)
    exactly equal value :     19  (0.4%)
    BACKWARDS           :      0  (0.0%)

  TRUE gap, in mean further guesses:
    all          median=1.0000  p90=5.0000
    clear        median=1.7500  p90=4.6667  frac truly close (<=0.25): 0.0%
    competitive  median=1.0000  p90=7.0000  frac truly close (<=0.25): 4.1%

  This is the finding that matters. v1's labels point the right way,
  but the pairs it calls `competitive` are separated by a median of a
  FULL GUESS of real value. v1's difficulty axis does not measure
  difficulty, so 'keep only the competitive pairs' would not have
  selected close decisions either.

